RELEVANT PROVISONS UNDER THE CODE OF CIVIL PROCEDURE, 1908 Section 107 :- Powers of Appellate Court.-- (1) Subject to such conditions and limitations as may be prescribed, an Appellate Court shall have power-- (a) to determine a case finally;
28 of 34 FAO-5934-2015 (O&M) -29- (b) to remand a case;
(c) to frame issues and refer them for trial;
(d) to take additional evidence or to require such evidence to be taken.
